text: ['({R/G} can be paid with either {R} or {G}.)\\nSacrifice Wild Cantor: Add one mana of any color.', "({R/G} can be paid with either {R} or {G}.)\\nTrample; haste; shroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", '({R/G} can be paid with either {R} or {G}.)\\n{3}{R}, Sacrifice a land: Gruul Guildmage deals 2 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\n{3}{G}: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', "({T}: Add {R} or {G}.)\\nAs Stomping Ground enters the battlefield, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters the battlefield tapped.", "({T}: Add {U} or {R}.)\\nAs Steam Vents enters the battlefield, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters the battlefield tapped.", "({T}: Add {W} or {B}.)\\nAs Godless Shrine enters the battlefield, you may pay 2 life. If you don't, it enters the battlefield tapped.", '({U/R} can be paid with either {U} or {R}.)\\nFlying\\nEach instant and sorcery spell you cast has replicate. The replicate cost is equal to its mana cost. (When you cast it, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)', "({U/R} can be paid with either {U} or {R}.)\\nWhen Petrahydrox becomes the target of a spell or ability, return Petrahydrox to its owner's hand.", '({U/R} can be paid with either {U} or {R}.)\\n{2}{U}: Copy target instant spell you control with mana value 2 or less. You may choose new targets for the copy.\\n{2}{R}: Copy target sorcery spell you control with mana value 2 or less. You may choose new targets for the copy.', '({W/B} can be paid with either {W} or {B}.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control.', '({W/B} can be paid with either {W} or {B}.)\\nFlying\\nWhenever Mourning Thrull deals damage, you gain that much life.', 'As long as equipped creature is tapped, tapped creatures you control get +2/+0.\\nAs long as equipped creature is untapped, untapped creatures you control get +0/+2.\\n{3}: You may tap or untap equipped creature.\\nEquip {3}', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, Rumbling Slum deals 1 damage to each player.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, each opponent loses 1 life. You gain life equal to the life lost this way.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, put it onto the battlefield. That creature gains haste until end of turn. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)', "Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nCreatures with power less than Battering Wurm's power can't block it.", "Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nCreatures with power less than Skarrgan Pit-Skulk's power can't block it.", "Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\nSacrifice Gristleback: You gain life equal to Gristleback's power.", "Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\n{2}{R}: Target creature can't block Burning-Tree Bloodscale this turn.\\n{2}{G}: Target creature blocks Burning-Tree Bloodscale this turn if able.", "Bloodthirst 1 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it.)\\n{R}, {T}: Attacking creatures get +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is Rabble-Rouser's power.", 'Bloodthirst 2 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nTrample', 'Bloodthirst 3 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.)', 'Bloodthirst 3 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nFlying\\n{R}{R}{R}: Return Skarrgan Firebird from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only if an opponent was dealt damage this turn.', 'Bloodthirst 3 (If an opponent was dealt damage this turn, this creature enters the battlefield with three +1/+1 counters on it.)\\n{1}, Sacrifice Skarrgan Skybreaker: It deals damage equal to its power to any target.', "Choose a card name. Until your next turn, spells with the chosen name can't be cast and lands with the chosen name can't be played.\\nDraw a card.", 'Choose one —\\n• Draw X cards.\\n• Invoke the Firemind deals X damage to any target.', 'Counter target nonblue spell.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {1}.\\nDraw a card.', 'Create X 1/1 white Pegasus creature tokens with flying, where X is your life total.', 'Creatures you control have trample.\\n{1}{R}{G}: Gruul War Plow becomes a 4/4 Juggernaut artifact creature until end of turn.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nAs Order of the Stars enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\nOrder of the Stars has protection from the chosen color.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhenever Souls of the Faultless is dealt combat damage, you gain that much life and attacking player loses that much life.", "Defender\\nWhenever Vertigo Spawn blocks a creature, tap that creature. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Destroy all enchantments target player controls.', 'Destroy each creature with mana value 3 or less.', 'Destroy target creature or enchantment.', 'Destroy target nonwhite, nonblack creature. Create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.\\nHaunt (When this spell card is put into a graveyard after resolving, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen the creature Seize the Soul haunts dies, destroy target nonwhite, nonblack creature. Create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Douse in Gloom deals 2 damage to target creature and you gain 2 life.', "Each land gets +2/+2 as long as it's a creature.", 'Electrolyze deals 2 damage divided as you choose among one or two targets.\\nDraw a card.', "Enchant creature\\nCreatures you control that are enchanted get +1/+1 and can't be blocked except by creatures with defender.", 'Enchant creature\\nCreatures you control that are enchanted get +1/+1 and have first strike.', "Enchant creature\\nCreatures you control that are enchanted get +1/+1.\\nIf a creature you control that's enchanted would die, return it to its owner's hand instead.", "Enchant creature\\nCreatures you control that are enchanted get +1/+1.\\nWhenever a creature you control that's enchanted becomes blocked, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each creature blocking it.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can\'t attack or block.\\nEnchanted creature has "At the beginning of your upkeep, you lose 1 life."', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has "{T}: This creature deals 1 damage to any target."\\n{1}{U}: Return Hypervolt Grasp to its owner\'s hand.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has "{T}: This creature deals damage equal to its power to target attacking or blocking creature."', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has first strike.\\n{1}{B}: Enchanted creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Enchant green creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +6/+6.\\n{G}{G}{G}, Sacrifice Wurmweaver Coil: Create a 6/6 green Wurm creature token.', "Exile each creature you control. Return those cards to the battlefield under their owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Exile target card from a graveyard.\\nDraw a card.', 'Exile target land.', 'First strike\\n{3}{G}: Ghor-Clan Bloodscale gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', 'Flash\\nEnchant creature\\nCreatures you control that are enchanted get +1/+1.', 'Flip a coin. If you win the flip, take an extra turn after this one.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, tap target creature.', "Flying\\nDaggerclaw Imp can't block.", 'Flying\\nHaunt (When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen Belfry Spirit enters the battlefield or the creature it haunts dies, create two 1/1 black Bat creature tokens with flying.', 'Flying\\nHaunt (When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen Blind Hunter enters the battlefield or the creature it haunts dies, target player loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.', 'Flying\\nHaunt (When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen Graven Dominator enters the battlefield or the creature it haunts dies, each other creature has base power and toughness 1/1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nStratozeppelid can block only creatures with flying.', 'Flying\\nWhen Angel of Despair enters the battlefield, destroy target permanent.', 'Flying\\nWhen Shrieking Grotesque enters the battlefield, if {B} was spent to cast it, target player discards a card.', 'Flying\\nWhen Skeletal Vampire enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 black Bat creature tokens with flying.\\n{3}{B}{B}, Sacrifice a Bat: Create two 1/1 black Bat creature tokens with flying.\\nSacrifice a Bat: Regenerate Skeletal Vampire.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sky Swallower enters the battlefield, target opponent gains control of all other permanents you control.', 'Flying\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Wee Dragonauts gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhenever you draw a card, Niv-Mizzet, the Firemind deals 1 damage to any target.\\n{T}: Draw a card.', 'Flying\\n{1}{R}: Torch Drake gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Gatherer of Graces gets +1/+1 for each Aura attached to it.\\nSacrifice an Aura: Regenerate Gatherer of Graces.', "Gruul Turf enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Gruul Turf enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {R}{G}.", 'Haunt (When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen Absolver Thrull enters the battlefield or the creature it haunts dies, destroy target enchantment.', 'Haunt (When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen Exhumer Thrull enters the battlefield or the creature it haunts dies, return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Haunt (When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen Orzhov Euthanist enters the battlefield or the creature it haunts dies, destroy target creature that was dealt damage this turn.', "Haunt (When this creature dies, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen Orzhov Pontiff enters the battlefield or the creature it haunts dies, choose one —\\n• Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.\\n• Creatures you don't control get -1/-1 until end of turn.", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nSilhana Ledgewalker can't be blocked except by creatures with flying.", "If Leyline of Lifeforce is in your opening hand, you may begin the game with it on the battlefield.\\nCreature spells can't be countered.", 'If Leyline of Lightning is in your opening hand, you may begin the game with it on the battlefield.\\nWhenever you cast a spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, Leyline of Lightning deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'If Leyline of Singularity is in your opening hand, you may begin the game with it on the battlefield.\\nAll nonland permanents are legendary.', 'If Leyline of the Meek is in your opening hand, you may begin the game with it on the battlefield.\\nCreature tokens get +1/+1.', "If Leyline of the Void is in your opening hand, you may begin the game with it on the battlefield.\\nIf a card would be put into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead.", "Izzet Boilerworks enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Izzet Boilerworks enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {U}{R}.", "Nonbasic landwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a nonbasic land.)", "Orzhov Basilica enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Orzhov Basilica enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {W}{B}.", "Parallectric Feedback deals damage to target spell's controller equal to that spell's mana value.", 'Prevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nAs Silhana Starfletcher enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\n{T}: Add one mana of the chosen color.', 'Replicate {1}{R} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nPyromatics deals 1 damage to any target.', "Replicate {1}{R} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nTarget Mountain becomes a 3/1 creature. It's still a land.", 'Replicate {1}{U} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost.)\\nDraw a card.', "Replicate {2}{U} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nReturn target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Replicate {2}{U} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost.)\\nCreate a 3/3 blue Weird creature token with defender and flying. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step.', "Replicate {3}{U} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nChoose target permanent an opponent controls. Search that player's library for a card with the same name and put it onto the battlefield under your control. Then that player shuffles.", 'Replicate {R} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nDestroy target artifact.', 'Replicate {U} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nTap target permanent.', 'Replicate {U}{R} (When you cast this spell, copy it for each time you paid its replicate cost. You may choose new targets for the copies.)\\nTarget creature gets +1/+0 and gains flying and first strike until end of turn.', "Return target nonland permanent with mana value X to its owner's hand.\\nDraw a card.", 'Sacrifice Goblin Flectomancer: You may change the targets of target instant or sorcery spell.', 'Sacrifice three white creatures: Exile target creature.\\nWhenever another black creature you control dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Savage Twister deals X damage to each creature.', "Skyrider Trainee has flying as long as it's enchanted.", 'Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains trample until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gets +4/+0 until end of turn. Another target creature gets -4/-0 until end of turn.', 'Target creature with flying loses flying until end of turn. Crash Landing deals damage to that creature equal to the number of Forests you control.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a nonland card from it and exile that card.', 'Target player discards a card.\\nHaunt (When this spell card is put into a graveyard after resolving, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen the creature Cry of Contrition haunts dies, target player discards a card.', "Target player draws two cards, then Cerebral Vortex deals damage to that player equal to the number of cards they've drawn this turn.", 'The next sorcery spell you cast this turn can be cast as though it had flash. (It can be cast any time you could cast an instant.)\\nDraw a card.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nBloodthirst X (This creature enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the damage dealt to your opponents this turn.)\\nProtection from instants", "This spell can't be countered.\\nDestroy target artifact or land.", 'Trample\\nWhenever Borborygmos deals combat damage to a player, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', 'Ulasht, the Hate Seed enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it for each other red creature you control and a +1/+1 counter on it for each other green creature you control.\\n{1}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Ulasht: Choose one —\\n• Ulasht deals 1 damage to target creature.\\n• Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', 'Untap all creatures you control.\\nDraw a card.', 'Vigilance\\n{4}{W}: Lionheart Maverick gets +1/+2 until end of turn.', "When Crystal Seer enters the battlefield, look at the top four cards of your library, then put them back in any order.\\n{4}{U}: Return Crystal Seer to its owner's hand.", "When Ghost Council of Orzhova enters the battlefield, target opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.\\n{1}, Sacrifice a creature: Exile Ghost Council of Orzhova. Return it to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'When Gruul Scrapper enters the battlefield, if {R} was spent to cast it, it gains haste until end of turn.', 'When Hatching Plans is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw three cards.', 'When Izzet Chronarch enters the battlefield, return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', "When Ogre Savant enters the battlefield, if {U} was spent to cast it, return target creature to its owner's hand.", "When Revenant Patriarch enters the battlefield, if {W} was spent to cast it, target player skips their next combat phase.\\nRevenant Patriarch can't block.", 'When Steamcore Weird enters the battlefield, if {R} was spent to cast it, it deals 2 damage to any target.', 'When Tin Street Hooligan enters the battlefield, if {G} was spent to cast it, destroy target artifact.', 'When Vedalken Plotter enters the battlefield, exchange control of target land you control and target land an opponent controls.', "Whenever Aetherplasm blocks a creature, you may return Aetherplasm to its owner's hand. If you do, you may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield blocking that creature.", "Whenever Bioplasm attacks, exile the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, Bioplasm gets +X/+Y until end of turn, where X is the exiled creature card's power and Y is its toughness.", 'Whenever Dune-Brood Nephilim deals combat damage to a player, create a 1/1 colorless Sand creature token for each land you control.', 'Whenever Glint-Eye Nephilim deals combat damage to a player, draw that many cards.\\n{1}, Discard a card: Glint-Eye Nephilim gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Whenever Smogsteed Rider attacks, each other attacking creature gains fear until end of turn. (They can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'Whenever Yore-Tiller Nephilim attacks, return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped and attacking.', 'Whenever a creature attacks you, its controller loses 1 life.', "Whenever a player activates an ability that isn't a mana ability, Burning-Tree Shaman deals 1 damage to that player.", 'Whenever a player casts an instant or sorcery spell, if that spell targets only Ink-Treader Nephilim, copy the spell for each other creature that spell could target. Each copy targets a different one of those creatures.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, that player sacrifices a permanent unless they pay {1}.', "Whenever an opponent discards a card, Abyssal Nocturnus gets +2/+2 and gains fear until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, its controller loses 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast a blue spell, target creature gains flying until end of turn.\\nWhenever you cast a red spell, Tibor and Lumia deals 1 damage to each creature without flying.', 'Whenever you cast a spell, you may put two +1/+1 counters on Witch-Maw Nephilim.\\nWhenever Witch-Maw Nephilim attacks, it gains trample until end of turn if its power is 10 or greater.', 'You gain 1 life for each player.\\nHaunt (When this spell card is put into a graveyard after resolving, exile it haunting target creature.)\\nWhen the creature Benediction of Moons haunts dies, you gain 1 life for each player.', "You may have creatures you control assign their combat damage this turn as though they weren't blocked.", '{1}, Exile two creature cards from your graveyard: Target player discards a card. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{B}.', '{2}, {T}: Exile target card from a graveyard.\\n{2}{W}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Moratorium Stone: Exile target nonland card from a graveyard, all other cards from graveyards with the same name as that card, and all permanents with that name.', '{2}{W}: Target player gains 1 life.\\n{2}{B}: Each player loses 1 life.', '{3}: Feral Animist gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is its power.', '{3}: Mizzium Transreliquat becomes a copy of target artifact until end of turn.\\n{1}{U}{R}: Mizzium Transreliquat becomes a copy of target artifact, except it has this ability.', "{3}{B}, {T}: Target creature gains swampwalk until end of turn. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)\\n{1}{B}: Regenerate Restless Bones.", '{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Destroy each creature with the same mana value as the sacrificed creature.', '{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', '{G}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 1 life.', '{R}, Sacrifice a creature: Scorched Rusalka deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.', "{R}: Gruul Nodorog gains menace until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by two or more creatures.)", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{U}{R}, {T}: Exile the top card of your library. Until your next turn, you may cast it if it's an instant or sorcery spell.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}{W}{B}, {T}: Target player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{R}{G}, {T}: Target creature gets +1/+1 and gains trample until end of turn.', '{T}: Gelectrode deals 1 damage to any target.\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, you may untap Gelectrode.', '{T}: Living Inferno deals damage equal to its power divided as you choose among any number of target creatures. Each of those creatures deals damage equal to its power to Living Inferno.', '{T}: Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{U}, Sacrifice a creature: Discard a card, then draw a card.', "{W}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature can't attack this turn.", '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', "{X}, {T}: Each creature with mana value X can't attack or block this turn."]
flavor: ['" . . . and you must also apply for an application license, file documents 136(iv) and 22-C and -D in triplicate, pay all requisite fees, request a . . ."', '"(Z—>)90° — (E—N²W)90°t = 1"', '"An entire order of mages who draw their power from Ravnica\'s smog? Yet another indicator of our world\'s decay."\\n—Dravash, dowsing shaman', '"But then . . . oh, but . . . which means . . . which would lead to . . . exactly!"', '"Crush them!"\\n—Borborygmos', '"Defense is as much a part of war as offense, the shield as important a tool as the sword."\\n—Alovnek, Boros guildmage', '"Diametrically opposing energies in self-sealed plasmodermic bubbles make great pets!"\\n—Trivaz, Izzet mage', '"Drakes? Bah! Things that breathe don\'t interest me. It breathes *fire*, you say? Well, that\'s a different story!"\\n—Zataz, Izzet clockwork artificer', '"Ever try to count hyperactive schoolchildren while someone shouts random numbers in your ear? It\'s like that."\\n—Geetra, frustrated mage', '"Fair? At what point in our negotiations did you convince yourself my goal was to be fair?"', '"Garb is for common folk. I prefer to wear insight and zeal, ambition and flame."', '"I fear to keep an open mind, for there are those who would use it as a door to my soul."\\n—Voka Schlak, Mauzam Asylum inmate, diary', '"I feel in them a sense of duty and commitment, yet I can feel nothing else. It is as if their duty is to an empty void."\\n—Razia', '"I ran the experiment through the brain of a schizophrenic lab-goblin. My burners\' flames fell asleep while the beakers jumped about and shattered. Success!"\\n—Myznar, Izzet psychomancer', '"I thought of fate as an iron lattice, intricate but rigidly unchangeable. That was until some force bent fate\'s bars to spare my life."\\n—Ilromov, traveling storyteller', '"I watched its blade swing through me, but I was hollow, empty. I saw its face contort in rage but could not hear it snarl."\\n—Klattic, Boros legionnaire', '"In secrecy is strength. None can oppose one who cannot be found."\\n—Szadek', '"It\'s easy to see why those Gruul dirtbags follow him—the only orders he gives are \'Crush them!\' and \'We eat!\'"\\n—Teysa', '"Look at her, once filled with innocence. Death has a way of wringing away such . . . deficiencies."\\n—Savra', '"Look to the old tomes, those bound in hides and written in yarberry ink. They hold the spells that can free us of the clutter of modern magecraft."\\n—Dravash, dowsing shaman', '"Looking out the great windows of Vitu-Ghazi at the foundry stacks belching their smoke to the sky, I wonder when the sky will take its vengeance."\\n—Heruj, Selesnya initiate', '"More horrible than their empty forms are their noble eyes. I dare not strike."\\n—Klattic, Boros legionnaire', '"Nature is the ultimate mindless destroyer, capable of power and ferocity no army can match, and the Gruul follow its example."\\n—Trigori, Azorius senator', '"No more wretched fate is there than to waste away. If you are slain, your ghost may at least avenge itself upon your killer. But what release is there for one slain by Time?"\\n—Ilromov, traveling storyteller', '"Of course I plan on going up. Kang here is the most trusted \'fin on the squad. Afraid? Me? No, I\'m just . . . waiting for the right wind conditions."', '"Our fealty to guilds dooms us. The old gods shall resurface. Our skins will wave upon the guild-masts over emptied streets, and our bones will clatter in the wind."\\n—Ilromov, traveling storyteller', '"Piece the tragic notes together and is it not a melody?"\\n—Teysa', '"Rauck-Chauv\'s like a holiday! Only it isn\'t on the calendars, and instead of dancing you knock people flat, and instead of giving gifts you break stuff."', '"Some gardeners sing to plants. I tell them stories—stories of how they once ruled the world, of the mortals who destroyed their kind, and of revenge."\\n—Bougrat, druid of the Cult of Yore', '"Steel rusts. Arrows break. But righteousness is always strong, always sharp."', '"Steering apparatus?! What for? Rip it out, sharpen it, and lash it to the front!"\\n—Ktank, Gruul plowmaster', '"Surprise is a useless, untidy emotion—the plaything of goblins and fools."', '"Take the bridge, men! Victory! Victory is ou— Retreat! RETREAT!"', '"The Golgari raise the bodies of their dead to serve. We raise the spirits of our dead to lead."', '"The blazekite is a simple concept, really—just a vehicular application of dragscoop ionics and electropropulsion magnetronics."\\n—Juzba, Izzet tinker', '"The call came, spell-borne through mortar and stone to the ear of every soldier. The call came, and the advantage was ours."\\n—Lodusz, captain of the watch', '"The first blow is the most important. It often negates the need for a second."\\n—Agrus Kos', '"The other guilds think they\'re untouchable. It\'s time we brought them back down to earth."\\n—Ghut Rak, Gruul guildmage', '"The sky isn\'t falling—it\'s being thrown at us!"\\n—Otak, Tin Street shopkeep', '"This palace will be our fire-spit, and roasted prince our victory meal. Send in the torch-pigs!"\\n—Ghut Rak, Gruul guildmage', '"We have no need for military might. We wield two of the sharpest swords ever forged: Faith in our left hand, Wealth in our right."\\n—Vuliev of the Ghost Council', '"We mourn our dead. We shroud our dead. We bury our dead. Too often, it seems, we must kill our dead again."\\n—Grazda, veteran armorer', '"We respect all lifeforms, but this one we respect from a distance."\\n—Mandor, Selesnya ranger', '"What is it? Um . . . what do you *want* it to be?"\\n—Juzba, Izzet tinker', '"When you hear thunder on a cloudless day, take cover and brace for the coming of the storm herd."\\n—Skotov, Tin Street basket vendor', '"Who truly runs this city? Look to the sky on hallowed days, and see whose sigil is stamped clearly onto the heavens."\\n—Vuliev of the Ghost Council', '"You can\'t have so many people living so close together, all practicing so much magic, and not expect some feedback."', '"You say that I am two-faced? Enough with the flattery. We have business to conduct."', '"Your deed cannot be undone. You, however, can be."\\n—Agosto, Azorius imperator', '"Your signet is no symbol of power. It marks only your need for numbers to aid you. What do you do, guild-rat, now that you face my blade alone?"', 'A skilled Izzet chronarch can carry out an epic vendetta between the fall of one hourglass grain and the next.', 'All that remains when the fog finishes are neat piles of polished bones, like acid-etched glass. Orzhov servants collect them to make altar chimes.', 'As stoic as the marble halls, as unblinking as the stars upon their shields.', 'At mealtimes, the Gruul customarily omit such niceties as using forks or killing the entrée.', "Cremation of the dead is not a religious ritual in Ravnica. It's a business designed to keep the Golgari from growing in numbers.", 'During their ascent to spirithood, patriarchs of Orzhova shed both flesh and emotion. This earthly slag is collected and formed into thrulls.', 'Each small blaze she sets jogs her memory, letting her piece together the mystery of her own fiery end.', 'From Tin Street to the Outcast Mansions, she walks unbidden and unbound, her graceful silence never shaken by the riot of city life around her.', 'Gruul shamans are bent on punishing the civilized. Any act more complex than rubbing sticks together or eating with utensils is met with the stinging burn of their magic.', 'Gruul territorial markings need not be legible. The blood, snot, and muck used to smear them are unmistakably Gruul.', 'He chanted over a pot of boiling blood and honey. His brain buzzed like a nest of hornets, and his muscles rippled with the might of the bear.', 'He ensures not only whether but also when and where the lightning strikes twice.', "He's an oxymoron.", 'His assistants calculate the amount of the tribute. He measures out the punishment for delinquency.', 'In light he finds both gift and weapon.', 'Instinct blood-tinted his world until he could see only one thing clearly: his prey.', "It departs through the streets' fissures with a sound like gravel pouring into a pond.", 'It tracks its victims by the scent of their breath, preferring to dine on those who recently ate well.', 'Its fickle form holds hints of a thousand former identities.', 'Izzet brains and Izzet boilers: contents under pressure.', 'Like many Izzet creations, weirds are based on wild contradictions yet somehow manage to work.', 'Loyal in battle, hearty in stew.', 'Lurking below the current, she thirsts until others come to drink.', 'Moon Market merchants sell a bottled scent to cutpurses and other criminals. Those doused in the liquid become "griffin bait."', "Niv-Mizzet's genius and vanity reverberate throughout the mirrored halls of Nivix.", 'One moment, conscious only of a sense of repose. The next moment, hearing the trudge of his own footsteps. He sighed and squinted into the glare ahead.', "Orzhov churches don't pass the plate for collection. They charge for admission.", 'Orzhov faithful file past to have their minds purged of "impure" desires. There, the guiltwardens eliminate any thoughts of hope or self-sufficiency.', 'Orzhov mage-sculptors bring their stone to life before they carve it. The shrieking begins as soon as the mouths are formed.', 'Orzhov prisoners are steeped in a blackened brew that robs their souls of strength. Patriarchs drink that brew to extend their own lives.', 'Petting the nodorog\\n—Gruul expression meaning "making a really big mistake"', 'Quyzl was told by his mentor to "make more time" for his studies.', 'Rakdos cultists hanged her for sport in the township square. Her ghost now stands vigil at what has become known as the Tree of Weeping.', "Rerouting magic through a goblin's brain is the surest way to throw it wildly off course.", 'Shadow lances are crafted from harvested souls. The more wicked the sinner, the keener the blade.', 'So wondrous to behold, so delicate and finely crafted—and yet, such a pleasure to smash.', "Some claim it's a failed Simic experiment, others say a Golgari creation. Both guilds deny all responsibility, while secretly studying its strange virulence.", 'Some use magic to spy through walls. Others use it to crush them.', 'Street folk call them "spire mice," but behind the mockery is an unspoken envy of the ledgewalkers\' skill at avoiding harm.', 'The "Days of Darkness" mark the stratozeppelids\' annual migration, when for five days they blot out the sun and trumpet their passing.', "The Gruul aren't satisfied with just smashing things. They continue smashing other things with the things they just smashed.", 'The Izzet learn something from every lesson they teach.', 'The Izzet signet is redesigned often, each time becoming closer to a vanity portrait of Niv-Mizzet.', 'The Orzhov contract the Izzet to animate slum districts and banish them to the wastes. The Gruul adopt them and send them back to the city for vengeance.', 'The Orzhov run a construction unit whose only business is rebuilding the wreckage left in the wake of wurms. When business is slow, they pay Golgari carnomancers to lure the wurms to the surface.', 'The Simic use the claws as scalpels, while the Rakdos use them for tattooing and torture. The Gruul use them to pick their teeth after lunching on the rest of the carcass.', 'The chant was interrupted, the components cooked, and Zok worried that it was his brain he smelled smoking.', 'The clouds grew thick, and then they grew teeth.', 'The eyes let flow with tears, then blood, then the very soul—the whole wrung inside out, dripping down into the blackened puddle of the past.', "The form of the sigil is just as important as the sigil itself. If it's carried on a medallion, its bearer is a master. If it's tattooed on the body, its bearer is a slave.", 'The snap of sinew. The crunch of bone. A cry for mercy. These are the music of the Gruul.', 'The soldier moved with fluid poise, his awareness extending far beyond five senses.', "They are the voice of the wild, crying out with nature's fury and bringing forth its primeval might.", 'They inflict pain to forget their own and break foes to feel whole.', 'To those in tune with the Firemind, there is no difference between knowledge and flame.', 'Tracing the horizon in a dance of wind and fire.', 'Two times the size, four times the smell.', "Unlike most churches, at Orzhova it's best to pray before you arrive.", 'When it awoke, it shattered the hillsides to make way for its passage.', 'When it awoke, it shook the plane with the thunder of its craving.', 'When it awoke, it spawned nameless thousands to herald its arrival.', 'When it awoke, the mirrors of the world reflected only darkness.', 'When it awoke, the worms of the earth hissed in a chorus of beckoning.', 'Where renown and solitude converge.', 'Where sovereignty and flesh converge.', 'Where storm and spellcraft converge.', 'Where strength and humility converge.', 'Where treachery and oblivion converge.', 'Which is worse—the sleep which never ends or that which never comes?', 'Would you trade the world for such a pet?', 'Zap on. Zap off.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Ben Thompson', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Dany Orizio', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Glen Angus', 'Glenn Fabry', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Hideaki Takamura', 'Ittoku', 'James Wong', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'John Avon', 'Jon Foster', 'Justin Norman', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Liam Sharp', 'Luca Zontini', 'Mark Romanoski', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Thompson', 'Mitch Cotie', 'Nick Percival', 'Nottsuo', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pat Lee', 'Pete Venters', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
